{"caseId":"OD2-HO-SEQ-1","answers":[{"itemId":"Q1","answer":"contradicted","confidence":85,"evidenceIds":["X9","E3","X8"]},{"itemId":"Q2","answer":"contradicted","confidence":75,"evidenceIds":["X9","E5","X8"]},{"itemId":"Q3","answer":"supported","confidence":80,"evidenceIds":["X8","X9","E2"]},{"itemId":"Q4","answer":"contradicted","confidence":80,"evidenceIds":["X9","E3","E2"]},{"itemId":"Q5","answer":"contradicted","confidence":75,"evidenceIds":["E2","X9","E5"]},{"itemId":"Q6","answer":"causal","confidence":70,"evidenceIds":["X8","X9","E2"]},{"itemId":"Q7","answer":"contradicted","confidence":70,"evidenceIds":["X9","X8","E5"]},{"itemId":"Q8","answer":"association-only","confidence":50,"evidenceIds":["E5"]},{"itemId":"Q9","answer":"contradicted","confidence":80,"evidenceIds":["X9"]},{"itemId":"Q10","answer":"preferred","confidence":75,"evidenceIds":["X8","X9"]},{"itemId":"Q11","answer":"harmful","confidence":85,"evidenceIds":["X9","E4","X8"]},{"itemId":"Q12","answer":"premature","confidence":70,"evidenceIds":["E5","X9"]},{"itemId":"Q13","answer":"acceptable","confidence":55,"evidenceIds":["X8","X9"]},{"itemId":"Q14","answer":"sufficient","confidence":70,"evidenceIds":["X8","X9"]}],"brief":"What is going on: the soft-pedal complaints are most likely caused by contaminated brake fluid, not by driving technique or the Tessaro pads. Northfield Motor Services renewed brake fluid on 11 Eastgate vans from a bulk drum that had taken on water. Two warranty vans (LK-217, LK-224) tested at 149–152°C boiling point against 255°C for sealed stock, and the garage's technician linked this to a soft pedal on long descents. All 11 vans that complained were Northfield-serviced. The two Northfield vans given fresh fluid did not complain. Drivers who complained also drove non-Northfield vans on Upper Wend with no reports, so the problem follows the van, not the driver.

How sure: moderately. The mechanism and the timing fit well, but no one has yet tested the other vans' fluid, and the Calder Road vans are unchecked.

What to do this week: take the Northfield-serviced vans out of service until their fluid is tested and renewed from sealed stock. Do not issue warnings or retrain drivers on this basis; that would suppress fault reports. Check the remaining Eastgate vans' fluid too. Hold the pad-supplier decision until its evidence is clearer.","methodChoice":"Evidence collected: X8 and X9 (2 of 2 allowed)."}
